      "id": 12182,
      "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
      "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-04T15:06:12.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I picked this up on Steam Early Access yesterday; I had wanted to Kickstart it, but I was unemployed during the drive, so I was unable to.</p><p>Darkest Dungeon is a Lovecraft-tinged medieval Rogue-like with a really unique \"Stress\" mechanic--in addition to managing your party's hit points, your heroes gain stress from crawling through undead-infested dungeons, which can lead to inter-party conflict and even total breakdowns. &nbsp;</p><p>I've done pretty well thusfar--I played last night for about 4 hours total, with no fatalities and no failed quests. &nbsp;Party balance is incredibly important, as is position within your party. &nbsp; It's a real challenge, but a ton of fun with great atmosphere; the voice-over alone is spectacular!</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:39.013Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
